.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OSSL_QUIC_CLIENT_METHOD 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_QUIC_client_method ,
.Nm OSSL_QUIC_client_thread_method ,
.Nm OSSL_QUIC_server_method
.Nd Provide SSL_METHOD objects for QUIC enabled functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/quic.h
.Ft const SSL_METHOD *
.Fo OSSL_QUIC_client_method
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft const SSL_METHOD *
.Fo OSSL_QUIC_client_thread_method
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft const SSL_METHOD *
.Fo OSSL_QUIC_server_method
.Fa void
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn OSSL_QUIC_client_method ,
.Fn OSSL_QUIC_client_thread_method ,
and
.Fn OSSL_QUIC_server_method
functions provide methods for the
.Xr SSL_CTX_new_ex 3
function to provide QUIC protocol support.
.Pp
The
.Fn OSSL_QUIC_client_thread_method
uses threads to allow for a blocking mode of operation and avoid the
need to return control to the OpenSSL library for processing time based
events.
The
.Fn OSSL_QUIC_client_method
does not use threads and depends on nonblocking mode of operation and
the application periodically calling SSL functions.
.Pp
The
.Fn OSSL_QUIC_server_method
provides server-side QUIC protocol support and must be used with the
.Xr SSL_new_listener 3
API. Attempting to use
.Fn OSSL_QUIC_server_method
with
.Xr SSL_new 3
will result in an error.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return pointers to the constant method objects.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr SSL_CTX_new_ex 3 ,
.Xr SSL_new_listener 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn OSSL_QUIC_client_method
and
.Fn OSSL_QUIC_client_thread_method
were added in OpenSSL 3.2.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_QUIC_server_method
was added in OpenSSL 3.5.
